---
import LearnLayout from "../../components/LearnLayout.astro";
---

<LearnLayout
  title="Save Your First Project — Learn — cntxt"
  description="How a browser window becomes a Project you can close and restore later."
  path="/learn/first-project"
>
  <a href="/learn" class="back-link">← Learn</a>
  <h1>Save your first Project</h1>
  <p>
    Every open window is already a Project — there's no "save" button to
    remember. Install cntxt and your current window becomes an "Untitled
    Project" automatically; rename it whenever you like. From then on, its
    tabs mirror live: open a tab, close a tab, move a tab — the Project
    updates itself, so it's never in an unsaved state.
  </p>
  <p>
    When you're done for now, close all of its tabs from the dashboard and
    the Project stays saved, ready to reopen later. Restoring puts its tabs
    back into the current window with one click.
  </p>

  <h2>Status</h2>
  <table class="status-table">
    <thead>
      <tr><th>Capability</th><th>Status</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr>
        <td>Save a window's tabs as a Project</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Live tab sync (a Project mirrors its window automatically)</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Close all tabs, keep the Project</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Restore a Project into the current window</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Resume your last-used Project/Group on browser startup</td>
        <td>🟢 Shipped</td>
      </tr>
      <tr>
        <td>Restore a Project alongside what's already open (a new window, not a replace)</td>
        <td>🔴 Planned</td>
      </tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
</LearnLayout>
